jsonTest -- THE JSON TREE, PINNED BY VALUE (SEQ 176/178, 2026-09-25)

testJSON drives JSONblock and prints the tree it hands back, two levels deep: the root's
member count, then each member's tag (the KEY), member count and value, then each member's
own members. addrOf prints each node's field and body number, so pop.sh can ask whether two
members are two nodes or one.

Why it prints the tree instead of ok/FAIL: until dc8b0b9 JSONfield returned its action
local (bear-trap #50) -- every member of every object shared ONE body, read back as N copies
of the last value, with no key -- and JSONarray yielded its last element in place of the
array. ok/FAIL could not see either: a wrong tree is still non-null. The pop.sh rows now
assert keys, values, counts and distinct bodies, and the old parked baseline row is retired
into them.

The empty-array case is pinned AS IT STANDS: it prints "nextGroup: ERROR JSONlist does not
contain a list" (JSONarray's `if JSONlist;` is an existence test that passes on the rule
itself -- bear-traps #26/#34, docs/fixIts.md F-99). Not chased; its row names it.

The collecting-action stroke of parse-then-fire step 2 moves JSONfield and JSONarray onto
the value-yield model; its certificate is that these rows stay green.

/*****************************************************************************
	2026-07-02 Google-fonts probe (M3, Fearless marching orders). The real
	`webfonts/v1/webfonts` API response wraps many font entries in a top-level
	"items" ARRAY OF OBJECTS: {"items":[{...},{...}]}. That shape currently
	FAILS cleanly (no crash, no hang - JSONblock reports a clean parse
	failure at the first array element). Root cause, from the grammar
	(incant/utilities): JSONarray's elements are JSONitem -> JSONtoken@, and
	JSONtoken's option list is only "false"/"true"/GrouP/NumbeR - it does NOT
	include JSONblock. So an array can hold strings/numbers/bools but not
	nested objects. A single flat font entry (the case just above, and every
	other case in this file) parses fine; it's specifically array-of-objects
	that chokes. Grammar fix (NOT done here - out of scope for this probe):
	add JSONblock as a JSONtoken option so array elements can be objects.
*****************************************************************************/
